# Architecture Layers (anti-patterns)

## Ownership

| Layer | Owns | Must not |
|---|---|---|
| `app/**/page.tsx` | Route, permission gate, server data fetch, compose feature UI | `'use client'`, fetch via browser client, fat UI |
| `features/<domain>/` | One backend/domain only (`fees`, `students`, `auth`, …) | Import another feature; become a dumping ground |
| `features/*/api/` | Typed `openapi-fetch` wrappers + query keys; always `unwrap` | UI, React hooks; local error/unwrap copies |
| `features/*/hooks/` | TanStack Query / domain logic; calls `api/` | JSX; untyped `data`/`error` |
| `features/*/components/` | Presentational / interactive UI for that domain | Call `lib/api` or `features/*/api` directly |
| `components/ui` | Primitives (shadcn) | Domain knowledge |
| `components/patterns` | Cross-feature widgets | Feature-specific API calls |
| `lib/*` | Shared infra (api client, auth, money) | Feature UI |

## Data flow (required)

```
page (RSC) → feature hook or server api helper → lib/api client → /api/proxy
                ↑
         client component only consumes hooks / props
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — API in a component
'use client';
export function InvoiceList() {
  const [rows, setRows] = useState([]);
  useEffect(() => { api.GET('/fees/invoices').then(...) }, []);
}

// ✅ GOOD — hook owns data; component renders
'use client';
export function InvoiceList() {
  const { data, isPending } = useInvoices(filters);
  if (isPending) return <Skeleton />;
  return <DataTable rows={data} />;
}
```

## Screens are server-first

- Default every `page.tsx` / `layout.tsx` to a **Server Component**.
- Push `'use client'` to the smallest leaf that needs state, effects, or browser APIs.
- Server page loads initial data (or passes ids); client children hydrate via hooks with that input.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
'use client';
export default function FeesPage() { return <FeesScreen />; }

// ✅ GOOD
export default async function FeesPage() {
  const user = await fetchSessionUser();
  return <FeesScreen campusId={user.campusIds[0]} />; // client island
}
```

## One job per component

- One concern: list, form, row actions, dialog — not all four.
- If a file mixes data fetching, form state, and layout, split into hook + presentational pieces.
- Name by role: `InvoiceTable`, `RecordPaymentDialog`, `useRecordPayment` — not `FeesStuff`.

## Typing

- Prefer OpenAPI-generated types from `src/lib/api/schema.ts`; Zod for forms/params.
- No `any`, `@ts-ignore`, or untyped fetch results. Props and hook returns must be explicit.
- `api/` helpers: explicit params and `Promise<Dto>` (unwrapped via `unwrap` from `@/lib/api/errors`).
- `hooks/`: TanStack Query generics — `useQuery<TData, ApiClientError>`, `useMutation<TData, ApiClientError, TVariables>`.
- Session-route helpers (login/2FA) return typed result unions in `types.ts`, not `unknown` blobs.
- Feature `types.ts` only for view models / aliases that OpenAPI does not already cover (or session shapes).

## Feature folder checklist

```
features/<domain>/
  api/          # one typed wrapper file per operation + keys.ts
  hooks/        # one typed hook file per useX → api/
  components/   # UI only; use hooks or props
  schemas.ts    # Zod
  types.ts      # optional view models / DTO aliases
  index.ts      # public barrel
```

New domain → new `features/<domain>`. Do not stretch `auth` or a random feature to hold unrelated modules.
